Facts and test values from other projects
-----------------------------------------

The KNX IP Secure, ETS keyring and ETS project specifications are
published to KNX Association members. The public facts this module uses
were read from two Python projects; no code was taken from either (see
PROVENANCE.md for what was read):

- xknx (github.com/XKNX/xknx, MIT, the XKNX authors; its LICENSE file
  names no copyright holder):xknx/secure/security_primitives.py and
  examples/ip_secure_calculations.py (KNX IP Secure key derivation,
  handshake MACs and the secure wrapper), xknx/secure/keyring.py (the
  keyring's key derivation, IV, password padding and signature, and from
  v0.2.0 its backbone, group key and sender elements),
  xknx/io/routing.py (routing flow control), xknx/io/ip_secure.py and
  xknx/knxip/timer_notify.py (KNX IP Secure routing and its timer),
  xknx/secure/data_secure.py and data_secure_asdu.py (KNX Data Secure).
  The KNX IP Secure test vectors in secure_test.go are the example values
  of examples/ip_secure_calculations.py; the TIMER_NOTIFY vectors in
  routing_test.go come from test/io_tests/secure_group_test.py, and the
  Data Secure vectors in datasecure_test.go from
  test/secure_tests/data_secure_test.py with keys of its ETS keyring
  SecureTest.knxkeys; all used under xknx's MIT licence.
- xknxproject (github.com/XKNX/xknxproject, GPL-2.0-only, the XKNX
  authors): xknxproject/zip/extractor.py and loader/project_loader.py
  and, from v0.2.0, loader/hardware_loader.py,
  loader/application_program_loader.py, util.py, models.py and
  combination/combination.py
  were read for facts only (the .knxproj archive layout, the product
  catalogue's program and group object references, the ETS 6
  project password derivation parameters, the 0.xml element and
  attribute names). Facts are not covered by its licence; no code,
  comment or structure of it is in this module.

Dependencies
